{
  "_id": "6a32bbf543b548b57e937f4e",
  "title": "CLIs and the Terminal",
  "slug": "clis-and-the-terminal",
  "type": "lesson",
  "description": "Learn what CLI apps are and how terminal commands work.",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "attrs": {
      "version": 1
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "7181770c-1f53-40bd-9e26-f7028e99c044",
          "data-toc-id": "7181770c-1f53-40bd-9e26-f7028e99c044",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "CLIs and the Terminal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If you followed our "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "/packs/javascript-foundations",
                  "target": "_blank",
                  "rel": "noopener noreferrer nofollow",
                  "class": null,
                  "title": null
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "lesson pack about JavaScript"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", you would have written JavaScript in the browser i.e. ran it on a web page or the browser console. A command-line app works differently. The user does not click buttons or submit forms. They type a command into the terminal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In this lesson pack, you will learn Node.js while building CLI apps. This is a project-based pack, so follow along and run the examples as you read. Each lesson builds a small tool or improves one from an earlier lesson."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "previewBoundary",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In this lesson, you will build a tiny command called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "where-am-i"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". It will print the folder where the command started. This will teach you about what CLI apps are, different parts, working directories and more."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "9f754603-fe3f-4a28-af58-4ae309b83725",
          "data-toc-id": "9f754603-fe3f-4a28-af58-4ae309b83725",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What a CLI app is"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "CLI stands for "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "command-line interface"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". A CLI app is a command-line program you control by typing commands."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In a browser app, the interface is the page i.e. user gives their input by interacting with buttons, links, and text fields. In a CLI app, the interface is the command line and the user interacts by using words. The program responds with text, files, or actions."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Here are some examples of the terminal commands:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "node app.js\nnpm install\ngit status"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In these examples, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "node"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "npm"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "git"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " are CLI apps. The words after the command are passed to the CLI app as input and tell it what to do."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "attrs": {
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "attrs": {
                  "textAlign": null,
                  "suggestion": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Read "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "node app.js"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " as: start Node.js and ask it to run "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "app.js"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "attrs": {
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "attrs": {
                  "textAlign": null,
                  "suggestion": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Read "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "npm install"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " as: start npm and ask it to install the packages for this project."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "attrs": {
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "attrs": {
                  "textAlign": null,
                  "suggestion": null
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Read "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "code"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "git status"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " as: start Git and ask it to show the current state of the repository."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "90211ea7-ec64-4081-bc50-b11855084b0b",
          "data-toc-id": "90211ea7-ec64-4081-bc50-b11855084b0b",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Commands have parts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Take a look at the command below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "node where-am-i.js"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The first word is the command name i.e. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "node"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and the next word is an argument i.e. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "where-am-i.js"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Commands can also have flags. In the example below:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "git status --short"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "git"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the command. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "status"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the action. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "--short"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a flag that asks Git to print a shorter version of the output."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "image",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "src": "https://assets.roadmap.sh/guest/cropped-bg6la.png",
          "alt": "",
          "title": "",
          "description": "",
          "width": "100%",
          "align": "left",
          "showCaption": false,
          "aspectRatio": "original",
          "originalAspectRatio": "1536/842"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "611706ef-7e52-4847-aee2-109b42252752",
          "data-toc-id": "611706ef-7e52-4847-aee2-109b42252752",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The terminal has a current folder"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When you run a command, it starts from a folder. That folder is called the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "current working directory"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This matters because many commands read or write files relative to that folder. If you run a command from your Desktop, it starts from your Desktop. If you move into a project folder, it starts from there."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Open your terminal and run the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "pwd"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " command and it will print the current working directory when you run the command."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "pwd"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On macOS and Linux, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "pwd"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " means \"print working directory\". PowerShell supports this too, so Windows users use the same command."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Move to another folder with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "cd"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ":"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "cd projects"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If you run "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "pwd"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " now, you will get the different output from before."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "237d8c4a-7ddf-4176-8efc-b1fe73735dd8",
          "data-toc-id": "237d8c4a-7ddf-4176-8efc-b1fe73735dd8",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Build where-am-i"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Create a file called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "where-am-i.js"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and put this code inside it:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "js"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "const currentFolder = process.cwd();\n\nconsole.log(`Current folder: ${currentFolder}`);"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The first line asks Node.js for the folder where the program started. The second line prints that folder."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The important part is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "process.cwd()"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Node.js provides a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "process"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " object to give your program information about the running process. We will look closer at "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "process"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in the next lesson. For now, remember that "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "process.cwd()"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " gives you the folder where the command started."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "74fa468b-c6cc-4eec-aa5e-2e8ab2ced1ea",
          "data-toc-id": "74fa468b-c6cc-4eec-aa5e-2e8ab2ced1ea",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Run the command"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Now run the file from your terminal using"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "node where-am-i.js"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You should see output like this:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "txt"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Current folder: /Users/ava/projects/cli-practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Your folder path will be different. The command prints the folder where you ran it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "id": "2f4a3609-2e87-4c80-9c2e-389ba5588a02",
          "data-toc-id": "2f4a3609-2e87-4c80-9c2e-389ba5588a02",
          "suggestion": null,
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Try it"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Create a new folder and move into it:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "mkdir cli-practice\ncd cli-practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Create a file called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "code"
              }
            ],
            "text": "where-am-i.js"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with this code:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "js"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "const currentFolder = process.cwd();\n\nconsole.log(`Current folder: ${currentFolder}`);"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Run it:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "node where-am-i.js"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Read the output. It shows the folder you are in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Now move up one folder:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "cd .."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Run the file again by giving Node.js the path:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "bash"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "node cli-practice/where-am-i.js"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The printed folder should change. The file is the same, but the command started from a different folder."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finally, edit the label in your file:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "codeBlock",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "language": "js"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "const currentFolder = process.cwd();\n\nconsole.log(`This command started in: ${currentFolder}`);"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Run the command again. You changed the JavaScript output, but the terminal command stayed the same."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "qaSection",
        "attrs": {
          "suggestion": null,
          "category": ""
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "07776f48-2140-4ab8-876e-7fa6d9fac611",
              "data-toc-id": "07776f48-2140-4ab8-876e-7fa6d9fac611",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Test Your Understanding"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "a35e676e-5884-4038-9e33-d8c3809649fb",
              "data-toc-id": "a35e676e-5884-4038-9e33-d8c3809649fb",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What is a CLI?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A CLI is a command-line interface. It is a program you control by typing commands into the terminal instead of clicking buttons on a screen. Tools like "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "npm"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", and "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "git"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " are CLI apps. You start them by typing their command name, then you pass extra words to tell them what work to do."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "68504438-6781-4521-ac67-ac8ead85e1c0",
              "data-toc-id": "68504438-6781-4521-ac67-ac8ead85e1c0",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Is "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "node where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " JavaScript syntax?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "No. "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "node where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " is a terminal command, not JavaScript syntax. The command starts the Node.js program and gives it a file named "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". Node.js then reads that file and runs the JavaScript inside it."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "7c808227-c89e-418e-8cb3-b7296ecf6062",
              "data-toc-id": "7c808227-c89e-418e-8cb3-b7296ecf6062",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What is the current working directory?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The current working directory is the folder where a command starts. When a CLI reads or writes files, it often uses this folder as its starting point. If you run the same command from a different folder, the command may read different files, write files somewhere else, or print a different path."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "adf9215a-9a51-4030-969c-5ec9f7c5b822",
              "data-toc-id": "adf9215a-9a51-4030-969c-5ec9f7c5b822",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What does "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "node"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " do in "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "node where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "node"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " starts the Node.js program. The next word, "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", is passed to Node.js as an argument. Node.js uses that argument as the JavaScript file to read and run."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "id": "20a974fe-df2f-43dd-b65c-edb860eb03f6",
              "data-toc-id": "20a974fe-df2f-43dd-b65c-edb860eb03f6",
              "suggestion": null,
              "level": 3
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What does "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "process.cwd()"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " give us?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "attrs": {
              "textAlign": null,
              "suggestion": null
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "process.cwd()"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " gives us the current working directory. In this lesson, it lets the "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ],
                "text": "where-am-i.js"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " script print the folder where the command started. We are not changing folders from JavaScript here. We are only asking Node.js to tell us where the command began."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
          "textAlign": null,
          "suggestion": null
        }
      }
    ]
